'' A PARAMETER WITH NEITHER KEYWORD IS NOT BYVAL. Measured from the signatures fbc
'' emits:
''
''   n as integer   int64 N$1          a as string    FBSTRING* A$1
''   d as double    double D$1         a as zstring   char* A$1
''   e as ENUM      $1E E$1            a as wstring   uint16* A$1
''   p as U ptr     struct $1U* P$1    a as ustring   FBUSTRING* A$1
''   u as U         struct $1U* U$1
''
'' -- BYREF for a UDT and for every string kind, BYVAL for everything else. And
'' 'z as zstring * 8' with no keyword is error 324, "Fixed-length string combined with
'' BYREF", which is fbc saying the default it chose there was byref.
''
'' tiko read the absence of the keyword as byval, so 'sub mut( u as U )' received a
'' COPY -- 'u.k = 99' wrote to it, the caller's object was unchanged, and nothing in
'' the IR said so. Every unannotated UDT and string parameter in the corpus and in the
'' shipped headers was passed the wrong way. check-mangle carries the rule too: 109
'' rows now, up from 102.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/param-default-byref.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void MUT(@a)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void MUTS(@t)
'' GOLDEN: expected/param-default-byref.out
